{"approaches":[{"name":"combine_instructions","fit":1,"reason":"Two compatible requirements applied in the same turn: the AGENTS.md one-sentence-answer rule and the user's request to put the answer in a file. The reply applied the one-sentence rule to the file, then delivered the explanation in chat anyway, so stating how the two combine targets the failure directly."},{"name":"correct_instruction","fit":2,"reason":"The reply cited the AGENTS.md one-sentence rule as the reason for its shape, so editing that rule to say the chat reply only acknowledges a requested file would fix it where it is stated."},{"name":"define_before_use","fit":2,"reason":"The reply read \"answer\" in the one-sentence rule as the file's content rather than the chat reply, so defining which output the rule governs would remove that misreading."},{"name":"give_exact_text","fit":3,"reason":"Giving the finished acknowledgement sentence to use when an answer goes to a file would stop the reply from writing its own quote and justification paragraphs."},{"name":"rewrite_instructions","fit":3,"reason":"Rewording the existing one-sentence rule to cover the file-delivery case could fix the conflation without adding new text, though it is less targeted than stating how the two combine."},{"name":"explain_consequence","fit":4,"reason":"Saying beside the rule that repeating the file's content in chat defeats the user's request for a file might discourage quoting it, but the agent's misreading of the rule's scope would remain."},{"name":"add_guidance","fit":4,"reason":"New guidance on acknowledging written files could help, but an existing rule already covers the length of answers, so editing that rule is better than adding parallel text."},{"name":"fix_load_trigger","fit":5,"reason":"The reply cited AGENTS.md by name, so the instruction was clearly loaded, and a trigger fix is unlikely to matter."},{"name":"one_form","fit":6,"reason":"Nothing in the evidence shows several competing forms of the acknowledgement for the agent to choose between."},{"name":"remove_copied_text","fit":6,"reason":"The reply quoted its own explanation, not an example or sample from the instructions, so there is no copied text to remove."},{"name":"copy_text_last","fit":7,"reason":"No command, path or value was miscopied, because answer.md was written correctly."}]}
```

